 <aside class="status" aria-label="GitHub and status update"><strong>GitHub and status update — 26 October 2026</strong><p><strong>RTA verifier review checkpoint:</strong> the separate VCP RTA repository now provides fixes and a fixed review target (<code>cc695fe</code>). Recorded first-party CI passed 809 regression and 15 separate historical tests per environment, while the 40-event evidence replay remains <strong>INDETERMINATE</strong>. This does not establish independent reproduction, full conformance or a new release. <a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-10-26-rta-verifier-checkpoint/">Read the RTA update and limits →</a> A <a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vcp-rta-reference/actions/runs/40263948191">separate first-party CI</a> also completed the unchanged published recipe from a fresh network clone through final assessment on Python 3.11 and 3.13.5; this is procedure validation, not independent reproduction.</p><p>The <a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vcp-spec/pull/16">VCP candidate schema and synthetic checker</a> and <a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vap-spec/pull/26">VAP three-valued verification proposal</a> have been incorporated as research. Experimental extensions and proposed repairs remain <strong>unadopted; independent third-party reproduction has not been established</strong>. VAP v1.2.0 is still Draft 3. VCP v1.2 is Released, with known integrity issues under review and full conformance to VAP unestablished. This website's code examples are not a native VCP conformance verifier.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vcp-sdk/releases/tag/v0.1.0">vcp-sdk v0.1.0</a> is a first-party pre-release offline core on GitHub, not a PyPI/npm release, an implementation of vcp-sdk-spec, or an independent external implementation. Its interpretation choices do not adopt normative changes.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vap-spec/blob/81fa81e01ef9418c3fb7a02ddfc7fd72d993b6b1/README.md#implementation-s