pdates</a></h3><p class="news-summary">Evidect #30–#34 add synthetic permission and receiver-state experiments. Latest first-party CI passed 306 tests per Ubuntu/macOS job. Extensions remain unadopted; independent…</p><details class="archive-record" id="github-update-20261102-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-github-update-20261102" class="status" style="scroll-margin-top:10rem"><h2 style="margin-top:0">2 November: five service-permission and receiver-history research updates</h2><p>Evidect #30–#34 add service-permission rechecks, saved ten-case verification, checkpoint expiry/generations/key revocation and challenge-bound checks against a separate store. Latest merged eeeacf7 passed 306 tests per Ubuntu/macOS first-party CI job (44 new + 262 existing).</p><p>These are same-controller synthetic experiments. Separate processes and keys do not establish independent administration; both-store rollback and other limits remain. Extensions are <strong>unadopted</strong>; independent third-party reproduction is <strong>not established</strong>. The 137-test record, earlier results and fixed distributions are preserved.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-02-service-permission-receiver-state/">Read the five updates and their limits →</a></p></section>
