ce updates</h2><p>Ten merged PRs cover cloud-evidence research, interop release preparation, Explorer dependency maintenance, local-settings guards and incident-source records. PR #61 is release preparation and was unpublished at the initial review. A later experimental prerelease at 12:09 JST on 8 November is recorded separately in the linked article. The research is unadopted; independent reproduction is not established. Test and CI records are first-party checks, not independent confirmation.</p><p>All cloud experiments are synthetic and operated by the same party; no live cloud calls were made. They do not prove Azure origin, complete observation, independent custody, latestness, third-party timestamps, power-loss durability or production readiness. A valid older snapshot can remain valid without a separately retained contradictory checkpoint. Verification of custody does not grant permission to publish evidence. First-party CI is not independent reproduction.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-08-cloud-evidence-maintenance-update/">Read the ten updates, CI and limitations</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="payment-research-20261107" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-07">2026-11-07</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-07-payment-evidence-research-update/">VSO publishes seven VAP payment-evidence research and AI design updates</a></h3><p class="news-summary">VAP #52–#58 cover payment evidence, dispatch recovery, two-person approval and collection, plus school-AI and consumer-agent design notes. First-party CI only; unadopted,…</p><details class="archive-record" id="payment-research-20261107-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-payme