<section id="original-github-update-20261102" class="status" style="scroll-margin-top:10rem"><h2 style="margin-top:0">2 November: five service-permission and receiver-history research updates</h2><p>Evidect #30–#34 add service-permission rechecks, saved ten-case verification, checkpoint expiry/generations/key revocation and challenge-bound checks against a separate store. Latest merged eeeacf7 passed 306 tests per Ubuntu/macOS first-party CI job (44 new + 262 existing).</p><p>These are same-controller synthetic experiments. Separate processes and keys do not establish independent administration; both-store rollback and other limits remain. Extensions are <strong>unadopted</strong>; independent third-party reproduction is <strong>not established</strong>. The 137-test record, earlier results and fixed distributions are preserved.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-02-service-permission-receiver-state/">Read the five updates and their limits →</a></p></section>
 </div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="github-update-20261101" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-01">2026-11-01</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-01-runtime-handoff-incident-review/">1 November: saved-report receiver verification and incident review</a></h3><p class="news-summary">Evidect #28 adds receiver verification; #29 documents incident sources and scope limits. First-party CI passed 137 tests and eight synthetic cases per OS. Extensions remain…</p><details class="archive-record" id="github-update-20261101-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-github-update-20261101" class="status" style="scroll-margin-top:10rem"><h2 style="margin-top:0">1 November: saved-report receiver verification and incident review</h2><p>Evidect #28 binds the signed observation handoff to original report bytes and recomputes summaries from saved observations. Each Ubuntu/macOS first-party CI passed 137 tests, including 27 new tests, and eight synthetic cases. PR #29 documents incident sources and scope limits; its three future test candidates remain unimplemented and untested.</p><p>Saved-evidence verification does not rerun the original operation or re-establish its authorization and original signatures. A narrow VALID is not a safety verdict. Extensions remain <strong>unadopted</strong>; independent third-party reproduction is <strong>not established</strong>. Historical 53-case, 159 / 26 and other records and fixed distributions are preserved.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-01-runtime-handoff-incident-review/">Read the two updates and their limits →</a></p></section>
 </div></details></div></li></ul></section><section class="archive-month" id="month-2026-10"><h2>2026-10</h2><ul class="news-list"><li class="news-row" id="github-update-20261031" data-news-record data-month="2026-10" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-10-31">2026-10-31</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-10-31-retention-runtime-interop-research-update/">31 October follow-up: post-approval changes, retention evidence and interoperability</a></h3><p class="news-summary">Three research areas: Evidect post-approval checks and process observations, VAP/Evidect retention review, and Python/Node interoperability. First-party CI only; extensions remain…</p><details class="archive-record" id="github-update-20261031-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-github-update-20261031" class="status" style="scroll-margin-top:10rem"><h2 style="margin-top:0">31 October follow-up: post-approval changes, retention evidence and interoperability</h2><p>Evidect #27 tests post-approval changes and process observations (37 existing + 43 new tests; eight synthetic cases). VAP #39–#41 and Evidect #22–#26 separate retention deadlines, deletion evidence and receiver review. VAP #1 adds Python/Node interoperability (32 test methods; two positive and six negative vectors). First-party CI counts remain separate by scope.</p><p>Process separation is not independent authority; a reached deadline or CLOSED_REVIEW does not establish deletion success. Proposals and experimental extensions remain <strong>unadopted</strong>; independent third-party reproduction is <strong>not established</strong>. Historical 53-case, 159 / 26 and other records and fixed distributions are preserved.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-10-31-retention-runtime-interop-research-update/">Read the three research areas and limits →</a></p></section>
